---
import ProjectPage from "../../layouts/ProjectPage.astro";
import StatGrid from "../../components/StatGrid.astro";

// FILLER: swap in the real network shape and inputs
const layers = [
  { name: "input", x: 110, color: "blue", labels: ["sensor 1", "sensor 2", "sensor 3", "sensor 4", "heading"] },
  { name: "hidden", x: 245, color: "mauve", labels: ["", "", "", "", "", ""] },
  { name: "output", x: 380, color: "teal", labels: ["left motor", "right motor"] },
];
const nodeFill: Record<string, string> = { blue: "fill-blue/20 stroke-blue", mauve: "fill-mauve/20 stroke-mauve", teal: "fill-teal/20 stroke-teal" };
const nodeText: Record<string, string> = { blue: "fill-blue", mauve: "fill-mauve", teal: "fill-teal" };
const height = 220;
const nodeY = (count: number, i: number) => 34 + ((height - 44) / count) * (i + 0.5);

// FILLER: swap in the real population size
const gaSteps = [
  { name: "spawn", detail: "50 robots" },
  { name: "simulate", detail: "run in Unity" },
  { name: "score", detail: "fitness" },
  { name: "evolve", detail: "select, mutate" },
];
const stepW = 105;
const stepX = (i: number) => i * (stepW + 20);
---

<ProjectPage
  slug="neural-network"
  title="Neural Network from Scratch"
  tagline="A neural network written from scratch in C#, with no ML libraries, and trained with a genetic algorithm to control swarm robots in a Unity simulation."
  tags={["C#", "Unity", "neural networks", "genetic algorithms"]}
  links={[{ label: "github", href: "https://github.com/marcoboone/Atombots_Simulation_ML_GA" }]}
>
  <!-- FILLER: swap in the real numbers -->
  <StatGrid
    stats={[
      { value: "0", label: "ML libraries" },
      { value: "5-6-2", label: "network shape" },
      { value: "50", label: "robots / generation" },
      { value: "200+", label: "generations" },
    ]}
  />

  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Each robot in the swarm is controlled by its own small neural network. The network reads the
      robot's sensors and outputs motor speeds. Instead of backpropagation, the networks are trained
      with a genetic algorithm: the best performers each generation are copied and mutated.
    </p>
  </section>

  <figure>
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 480 ${height}`} class="w-full h-auto" role="img" aria-label="Diagram of the network's input, hidden, and output layers">
      {
        layers.slice(0, -1).map((layer, l) => {
          const next = layers[l + 1];
          return layer.labels.map((_, i) =>
            next.labels.map((_, j) => (
              <line
                x1={layer.x}
                y1={nodeY(layer.labels.length, i)}
                x2={next.x}
                y2={nodeY(next.labels.length, j)}
                class="stroke-overlay1"
                stroke-opacity="0.6"
              />
            ))
          );
        })
      }
      {
        layers.map((layer, l) => (
          <g>
            <text x={layer.x} y="14" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" class={nodeText[layer.color]}>{layer.name}</text>
            {layer.labels.map((label, i) => {
              const y = nodeY(layer.labels.length, i);
              return (
                <g>
                  <circle cx={layer.x} cy={y} r="10" class="fill-crust" />
                  <circle cx={layer.x} cy={y} r="10" class={nodeFill[layer.color]} stroke-width="2" />
                  {l === 0 && <text x={layer.x - 18} y={y + 4} text-anchor="end" font-size="12" class="fill-subtext1">{label}</text>}
                  {l === 2 && <text x={layer.x + 18} y={y + 4} font-size="12" class="fill-subtext1">{label}</text>}
                </g>
              );
            })}
          </g>
        ))
      }
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Sensor readings go in, motor speeds come out. Every line is a weight in a hand-written matrix.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section>
    <h2>Training with a genetic algorithm</h2>
    <p>
      Every generation, each robot is scored on how well it does its task. The top robots survive,
      and their weights and biases are copied and randomly mutated to make the next generation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <figure>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 480 140" class="w-full h-auto" role="img" aria-label="Genetic algorithm training loop">
      <defs>
        <marker id="ga-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="fill-subtext0" />
        </marker>
        <marker id="ga-arrow-loop" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="fill-yellow" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      {
        gaSteps.map((step, i) => (
          <g>
            <rect x={stepX(i)} y="10" width={stepW} height="54" rx="5" class="fill-surface0 stroke-teal" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x={stepX(i) + stepW / 2} y="33" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" class="fill-text">{step.name}</text>
            <text x={stepX(i) + stepW / 2} y="51" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" class="fill-subtext0">{step.detail}</text>
            {i < gaSteps.length - 1 && (
              <line x1={stepX(i) + stepW} y1="37" x2={stepX(i + 1) - 2} y2="37" class="stroke-subtext0" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ga-arrow)" />
            )}
          </g>
        ))
      }
      <path
        d={`M${stepX(3) + stepW / 2},64 V100 H${stepX(0) + stepW / 2} V66`}
        fill="none"
        stroke-dasharray="5 3"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        class="stroke-yellow"
        marker-end="url(#ga-arrow-loop)"
      />
      <text x="240" y="124" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" class="fill-yellow">repeat for the next generation</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>The training loop repeats until the swarm's behavior stops improving.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section>
    <h2>Key features</h2>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>Custom matrix math and forward propagation, no ML libraries</li>
      <li>Genetic algorithm mutates weights and biases each generation</li>
      <!-- FILLER -->
      <li>Fitness function rewards reaching the goal and penalizes collisions</li>
      <li>Simulated in Unity so a whole generation runs in parallel</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Results</h2>
    <!-- FILLER: add a GIF or chart of fitness over generations -->
    <p>
      Early generations wander randomly. After a few hundred generations, the robots learn to move
      toward the goal and avoid each other.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProjectPage>
